
# <type>: <subject> - <flag>
# |<--------  maximum of 50 characters  -------->|

# <body>
# Provide a detailed description of this change. Wrap text over
# multiple lines as needed.
# |<------------   maximum line length of 72 characters   ------------>|

# <footer>
# Optional footers. Uncomment as needed.
#Refs: #<issue>
#Closes: #<issue>

#===============================================================================
# <type> can be:
#   - feature      A new, changed, or removed user-facing operation or behavior.
#   - performance  Optimization of the system's runtime performance.
#   - fix          A fix for a bug, error, regression, or incident.
#   - step         An increment toward implementing a larger change.
#   - refactor     An improvement to the internal design of the software.
#   - format       Low-level code formatting improvements.
#   - maintenance  A routine housekeeping task - dependencies, tool config, etc.
#   - chore        A small, insignificant change to non-production artifacts.
#   - release      Marks a new numbered version of the software.
#   - merge        An explicit merge commmit.
#   - revert       Reverts an earlier commit.
#
# <flag> can be:
#   - WIP          Work-in-progress that breaks the build.
#   - BREAKING     A breaking change to an external API.
#   - INCOMPAT     Internal breaking API change.
#   - EXPERIMENT   A code experiment.
#   - TEMPORARY    A temporary commit that will be reverted.
#
# Tips:
#   - Do not capitalize the subject line.
#   - Use the imperative mood in the subject line.
#   - Do not end the subject line with a period.
#   - Separate subject from body with a single blank line.
#   - Use the body to explain what and why, not how.
#   - Use "-" for bullet points in the body.
#===============================================================================
